    }\n```\n\nActual exception occurs in this method (of the 'Project' model):\n\n``` php\n    public static function getExisting()\n    {\n        return static::find()\n            ->where(['is_deleted' => false])\n            ->orderBy(['id' => SORT_DESC])\n            ->all();\n    }\n```\n\nmigration for this field:\n\n``` php\n    public function safeUp()\n    {\n        $this->addColumn('{{%project}}', 'is_deleted', Schema::TYPE_BOOLEAN . ' NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE');\n    }\n\n    public function safeDown()\n    {\n        $this->dropColumn('{{%project}}', 'is_deleted');\n    }\n```\n\nException:\n\n```\n1) frontend\\tests\\unit\\models\\ProjectTest::testCorrectDeleteProject\nyii\\db\\Exception: SQLSTATE[42883]: Undefined function: 7 ERROR:  operator does not exist: boolean = integer\nLINE 1: SELECT * FROM \"project\" WHERE \"is_deleted\"=0 ORDER BY \"id\" D...\n                                                  ^\nHINT:  No operator matches the given name and argument type(s). You might need to add explicit type casts.\nThe SQL being executed was: SELECT * FROM \"project\" WHERE \"is_deleted\"= ORDER BY \"id\" DESC\n```\n\nCalling the same method from the web part action works well.\n(I'm using advanced template).\nWhen I replace field type to Scheme::TYPE_SMALLINT test passes correctly.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/4672/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/4672/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":151646101,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUxNjQ2MTAx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/events/151646101","actor":{"login":"cebe","id":189796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTc5Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe","htm